{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat README.md && ls -ld ~/.codex ~/.codex/auth.json 2>/dev/null && codex exec --help | rg -n 'config|home|output-last|sandbox' | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 39 valentinakoniukhova  staff  1248 Nov  9 23:41 /Users/valentinakoniukhova/.codex\n-rw-------@  1 valentinakoniukhova  staff  3877 Nov  4 20:11 /Users/valentinakoniukhova/.codex/auth.json\n19:  -c, --config <key=value>\n20:          Override a configuration value that would otherwise be loaded from `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n24:          Examples: - `-c model=\"o3\"` - `-c 'sandbox_permissions=[\"disk-full-read-access\"]'` - `-c\n33:      --strict-config\n34:          Error out when config.toml contains fields that are not recognized by this version of\n48:          will use config default or show selection\n51:          Layer $CODEX_HOME/<name>.config.toml on top of the base user config\n53:  -s, --sandbox <SANDBOX_MODE>\n54:          Select the sandbox policy to use when executing model-generated shell commands\n59:          Route approval requests through automatic review using the workspace-write sandbox\n61:      --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\n62:          Skip all confirmation prompts and execute commands without sandboxing. EXTREMELY\n63:          DANGEROUS. Intended solely for running in environments that are externally sandboxed\n87:      --ignore-user-config\n88:          Do not load `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml`; auth still uses `CODEX_HOME`\n105:  -o, --output-last-message <FILE>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
